---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Platform | Roy Li for Richmond">
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Platform</div><h1>A practical agenda for Richmond.</h1><p class="lead">These are draft pillars for the first version of the site. They can be expanded into full policy pages as the campaign develops.</p></section>
    <section class="content">
      <h2>1. Safer neighbourhoods</h2><p>Prioritize everyday safety: streets, community spaces, traffic hotspots, and responsive local services.</p>
      <h2>2. Fiscal discipline</h2><p>Respect taxpayers by demanding clearer budgeting, measurable outcomes, and honest explanations of tradeoffs.</p>
      <h2>3. Better planning and housing realism</h2><p>Support growth that is practical, infrastructure-aware, and respectful of the people who already live and work here.</p>
      <h2>4. Small business and local economy</h2><p>Reduce friction where City Hall can help: permitting, communication, streetscape access, parking, and local commercial vitality.</p>
      <h2>5. Transparent governance</h2><p>Make decisions easier to follow, documents easier to understand, and elected officials easier to reach.</p>
      <h2>6. Real representation</h2><p>Representation cannot stop at identity. It must become access, influence, responsiveness, and visible results.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
